nodecode-financial-datasets is a rewrite of financial-datasets's financial-datasets/hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/financial-datasets/hermes-plugin
  commit 6745cb6261f86895364579d897be2b6067f117f1
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Financial Datasets, Inc. (LICENSE)

The original is a Python plugin for a harness: a manifest declaring 28 tools
(fd_ prefixed, so they cannot collide), a JSON schema for each, one handler per
tool over the Financial Datasets REST API, and a standard-library HTTP client
that sends the key in an X-API-KEY header, follows the API's next_page_url
paging, and normalizes the arguments the API reads (a ticker upper-cased, a
filer CIK zero-padded, a true flag spelled true). All of that is rewritten here
in Common Lisp: api.lisp is that client and the query it builds, its tool table
carries the same 28 names, routes, arguments, defaults and enumerations, and
cell.lisp declares the config section, the registrations, the /financial
command and one manual topic. The API, its routes, its arguments and its data
are Financial Datasets', unchanged.

What was left out, and why: the harness-specific packaging (the plugin
manifest, the install-time prompt that writes the key into an .env file, the
Python test suite) is replaced by the cell's own config section, which is how a
Nodecode cell declares its settings, and the key may also come from the
environment variable the section names. The tool descriptions are kept but
shortened to the guidance a model needs, since each one rides every request;
the JSON schemas keep every argument name, type, default, range and
enumeration the original declared. Nothing else of the original was dropped: no
tool, no route and no argument is missing.
